meta {
  name: Create Relationship
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/relationships
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "WC Test Relationship"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
  res.body.data.name: eq WC Test Relationship
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-15 on "David's Dev Account". **Major finding**:
  Relationships (relationship *types*, e.g. "Bundles"/"Cross-sell") were
  confirmed **read-only** in Phase 3 (quirk #38 -- "genuinely read-only,
  `API V3.md` says types are configured in the web app dashboard, not
  this API"). The 2026-09-15 `openapi_pimv3.json` refresh adds `POST
  /relationships` (and `PATCH`/`DELETE /relationships/{identifier}`) for
  the first time -- a **new** capability. Confirmed live: it genuinely
  works now, contradicting `API V3.md`'s dashboard-only claim.

  ## What it does
  `POST /relationships` with just `{"name": "..."}` -- `201 Created`.
  `RelationshipCreateInputDto` accepts only `name` -- `label` is
  auto-derived (slugified from the name, e.g. "WC Test Relationship" ->
  `wc_test_relationship`) and `status` defaults to `"ACTIVE"`; neither is
  settable on create.

  ## Not idempotent to re-run
  Relationship names are unique per account, enforced with **`409`**
  (`AlreadyExists` family, same side of the split as products/attributes/
  channels/families per quirk #25a/#33/#45a): `{"errors":[{"name":
  "AlreadyExists","description":"A Relationship with same name already
  exists"}]}`.

  ## Not kept as a fixture
  This relationship was renamed and deleted in the same session (see
  "Update and Delete Relationship.bru"); a second one
  ("WC Test Product Relationship") was created and used to test the new
  product-to-product linking endpoints, then also cleaned up -- see
  `17-Product-Relationships/`.
}

example {
  name: 201 - Success
  description: Real response captured 2026-09-15 on "David's Dev Account" -- this relationship was renamed and deleted later in the same session, not kept as a fixture.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/relationships
    method: post
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "name": "WC Test Relationship"
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 201
      text: Created
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "id": "6aa97b0ca30ca5945169a23c",
            "account_id": "6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c",
            "name": "WC Test Relationship",
            "label": "wc_test_relationship",
            "status": "ACTIVE",
            "created": "2026-09-15T17:06:20.283000",
            "modified": "2026-09-15T17:06:20.284000"
          },
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: 409 - Duplicate Name
  description: Real response captured 2026-09-15, re-creating a relationship with a name that already existed in this account at the time.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/relationships
    method: post
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "name": "WC Test Relationship"
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 409
      text: Conflict
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [],
          "errors": [
            {
              "name": "AlreadyExists",
              "description": "A Relationship with same name already exists"
            }
          ]
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
